      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Blue Sky Property are delighted to bring to the market this exceptional, fully restored three-bedroom mid-terrace Victorian residence, superbly positioned along the waterfront in the highly sought-after seaside village of Blackrock, Co. Louth.\r\n\r\nOriginally built with character and charm, this beautiful period home has been thoughtfully restored while retaining a wealth of original Victorian features, including traditional old tiles, solid timber flooring and cast iron radiators, creating a wonderful blend of historic character and comfortable modern living.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 119 sq. m., the accommodation is arranged over two floors and takes full advantage of its spectacular waterfront position, with uninterrupted views across Dundalk Bay towards the Cooley Mountains.\r\n\r\nThe first floor comprises a welcoming entrance hall, utility room, two bedrooms and a generous family bathroom. The principal bedroom is particularly impressive and enjoys the benefit of the property's elevated coastal outlook. A second bedroom and spacious bathroom complete this level.\r\n\r\nThe second floor provides the main living accommodation and comprises a bright and generously proportioned living room, separate dining room, kitchen, third bedroom, hall and additional bathroom. The living room offers stunning views across the bay, while the adjoining dining room provides an ideal space for entertaining. The kitchen is well positioned alongside the dining and living accommodation, creating a practical and sociable layout.\r\n\r\nThe property further benefits from a rear terrace patio and raised garden, providing a wonderful outdoor space for alfresco dining, entertaining or simply sitting back and enjoying the spectacular coastal views and sunsets.\r\n\r\nThis is a truly unique opportunity to acquire a fully restored Victorian residence in an exceptional waterfront setting. Combining original period features, generous accommodation and some of the finest coastal views in Blackrock, this beautiful home offers the opportunity to enjoy village living in one of County Louth's most desirable locations.\r\n\r\nLocation:\r\nBlackrock is one of County Louth's most desirable coastal villages, renowned for its beautiful beach, picturesque promenade and welcoming community. The waterfront is lined with cafés, restaurants, boutiques and everyday amenities, while the village also benefits from excellent primary schools and sporting facilities.\r\n\r\nDundalk Golf Club and the Fairways Hotel are both within easy reach, while Dundalk town centre is approximately a 10-minute drive away. The M1 motorway provides convenient access to both Dublin and Belfast, making Blackrock an ideal base for commuters and families seeking a combination of coastal living, character and connectivity.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBlue Sky Property and their servants or agents assume no responsibility for and give no guarantees, undertakings or warranties concerning the accuracy, completeness or up to date nature of the information and do not accept any liability whatsoever arising from any errors or omissions. The information does not constitute or form part of a contract and cannot be relied on as a representation of fact. Subject to contract / contract denied. Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
